<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Task>
    <Title>PHP - Bounded YARA-X Discovery - Windows</Title>
    <Description>&lt;P&gt;Finds PHP runtime versions in local application folders without executing PHP. The default checks standard PHP executable/module names: php, php-cgi, php-fpm, phpdbg, lsphp, frankenphp, libphp and mod_php, including version suffixes, Windows .exe/.dll and Linux .so/.so.N files. PHP DLLs are retained because the PHP core and Apache module can reside there. Ordinary .php scripts, documents, archives, media and unrelated binary names are outside the default runtime scan. Enable renamed/nonstandard binaries to inspect other native binaries; enable build text for optional source/build evidence.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Application folders in user profiles remain included, including Herd, Scoop and AppData programs. OS/recovery trees, known caches, backups and personal media are skipped by default; the broader-locations option restores these soft exclusions. Network storage, cloud placeholders, symlinks, containers, snapshots and BigFix scanner/cache files remain excluded. Archives/images are not unpacked. Files at or above 512 MiB are skipped by default. Limits or meaningful read failures produce a partial scan, preserving positive findings. BigFix reports success when the scan produces a new result, including partial coverage or no PHP found. Failed means the attempt could not produce a new usable scan result.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Analysis has four properties. TRUE means an upstream-affected PHP runtime version was detected for CVE-2026-109618/109619 (fixed upstream: 8.2.35, 8.3.36, 8.4.27, 8.5.12). FALSE means none detected in the checked scope, not proof of absence or lack of web exposure. Vendor backports can retain an older version and require vendor/package verification. Build text alone does not set TRUE. Partial results are identified beside the last scan time; while a scan runs the properties retain the previous finished scan.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Detailed scan log:&lt;/STRONG&gt; YARA_PHP/scan.log under the BigFix client state root: normally C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\YARA_PHP on Windows and /var/opt/BESClient/YARA_PHP on Linux. summary.txt supplies the four Analysis properties; scan.lock prevents overlapping scans. Temporary work files are removed after the action.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Minimum BigFix Client:&lt;/STRONG&gt; 9.5.7. Use a client release that supports your operating system.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Linux uses Bash 4+, GNU find/coreutils, awk, tar/gzip and flock (util-linux), with a prerequisite check; it does not need Python, jq, PHP or a compiler and installs no runtime. Windows uses PowerShell 5.1/.NET already supplied by supported Windows versions. Both use the pinned YARA-X engine delivered by BigFix. The action waits for completion. Rule source: https://github.com/bigfix/Site_Rapid_Response (Apache-2.0), an unofficial community utility rather than HCL-supported patch content.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Scan settings&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommended: leave the defaults unchanged.&lt;/strong&gt; Defaults cover typical workstations and servers while using low resource priority. Large developer or file servers may need higher limits. Increasing a limit can increase disk activity and run time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;What this setting does&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"&gt;Additional directory exclusions (comma-separated)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" value="" size="48" maxlength="4096" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Skip your chosen folders; leave blank for no additional exclusions. See the examples below.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"&gt;Include renamed or nonstandard PHP binaries (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"  /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Scans other native binary names; leaving this off can miss renamed or custom embedded PHP.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"&gt;Include OS, recovery, cache and data locations (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"  /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Restores OS, recovery, cache and data locations normally excluded, while retaining scan limits.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPIncludeBuildText"&gt;Include PHP source/build text (slower)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPIncludeBuildText"  /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Includes PHP build/header evidence without treating it as an installed runtime.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPEnumerationSeconds"&gt;File search time (minutes)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPEnumerationSeconds" value="20" size="12" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Stops searching after this many minutes and marks unfinished coverage as partial. (Allowed: 1 to 60.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPScanSeconds"&gt;Content scan time (minutes)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPScanSeconds" value="15" size="12" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Limits YARA content scanning to this many minutes and reports partial results if it times out. (Allowed: 1 to 60.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPMaxFiles"&gt;Maximum files checked&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPMaxFiles" value="5000000" size="12" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Caps files considered during discovery to bound work on unusually large filesystems. (Allowed: 1000 to 5000000.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPCandidateGB"&gt;Maximum candidate input (GiB)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPCandidateGB" value="30" size="12" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Caps the combined size of files sent to YARA; exceeding this reports a partial scan. (Allowed: 1 to 100.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPMaxFileMB"&gt;Maximum individual file size (MiB)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPMaxFileMB" value="512" size="12" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Skips individual files at or above this size; 512 MiB covers normal PHP and large embedded builds. (Allowed: 16 to 2048.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPCpuLimit"&gt;YARA CPU setting (%)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input id="PHPCpuLimit" value="10" size="12" /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Sets the YARA engine CPU target; this is not a total system CPU guarantee. (Allowed: 1 to 50.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;label for="PHPGentleDisk"&gt;Extra-gentle disk access (slower, Windows only)&lt;/label&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;input type="checkbox" id="PHPGentleDisk"  /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Uses lower disk scheduling priority to reduce disk contention, which can slow the scan.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exclusion examples:&lt;/strong&gt; Linux: &lt;code&gt;/data/*&lt;/code&gt; skips /data and every subfolder; &lt;code&gt;/data/&lt;/code&gt; skips only files directly in /data and still searches its subfolders; &lt;code&gt;*/data/*&lt;/code&gt; skips every folder named data and its subfolders. Windows equivalents: &lt;code&gt;C:\folder\*&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;C:\folder\&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;*\folder\*&lt;/code&gt;. Use absolute paths or a leading */; * matches any characters, including separators. Other characters are literal. Windows matching ignores case; Linux matching is case-sensitive. Separate entries with commas, without quotes. Spaces inside paths are supported; commas inside folder names are not. Maximum 32 entries and 4096 UTF-8 bytes. These exclusions also apply when broader locations are enabled and can hide PHP in the excluded scope; the scan log records them. Intentional exclusions do not mark a scan partial.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;button onclick="return PhpScan.prepare();"&gt;Configure and Take Action&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This passes only the selected settings to this Task's native Action1 and opens the standard Console Take Action dialog. Select computers there. The controls apply to this action only; the scanner script is stored in the Actions tab. API/WebUI actions without parameters use the defaults; API integrations can supply the same action parameters. CPU is a YARA engine setting, not a total-host CPU guarantee.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;script type="text/javascript"&gt;var phpScanFields = [{"key": "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex", "label": "Additional directory exclusions (comma-separated)", "default": "x", "text": true, "help": "Skip your chosen folders; leave blank for no additional exclusions. See the examples below."}, {"key": "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames", "label": "Include renamed or nonstandard PHP binaries (slower)", "default": 0, "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true, "help": "Scans other native binary names; leaving this off can miss renamed or custom embedded PHP."}, {"key": "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations", "label": "Include OS, recovery, cache and data locations (slower)", "default": 0, "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true, "help": "Restores OS, recovery, cache and data locations normally excluded, while retaining scan limits."}, {"key": "PHPIncludeBuildText", "label": "Include PHP source/build text (slower)", "default": 0, "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true, "help": "Includes PHP build/header evidence without treating it as an installed runtime."}, {"key": "PHPEnumerationSeconds", "label": "File search time (minutes)", "default": 1200, "min": 30, "max": 3600, "multiplier": 60, "help": "Stops searching after this many minutes and marks unfinished coverage as partial."}, {"key": "PHPScanSeconds", "label": "Content scan time (minutes)", "default": 900, "min": 30, "max": 3600, "multiplier": 60, "help": "Limits YARA content scanning to this many minutes and reports partial results if it times out."}, {"key": "PHPMaxFiles", "label": "Maximum files checked", "default": 5000000, "min": 1000, "max": 5000000, "help": "Caps files considered during discovery to bound work on unusually large filesystems."}, {"key": "PHPCandidateGB", "label": "Maximum candidate input (GiB)", "default": 30, "min": 1, "max": 100, "help": "Caps the combined size of files sent to YARA; exceeding this reports a partial scan."}, {"key": "PHPMaxFileMB", "label": "Maximum individual file size (MiB)", "default": 512, "min": 16, "max": 2048, "help": "Skips individual files at or above this size; 512 MiB covers normal PHP and large embedded builds."}, {"key": "PHPCpuLimit", "label": "YARA CPU setting (%)", "default": 10, "min": 1, "max": 50, "help": "Sets the YARA engine CPU target; this is not a total system CPU guarantee."}, {"key": "PHPGentleDisk", "label": "Extra-gentle disk access (slower, Windows only)", "default": 0, "min": 0, "max": 1, "checkbox": true, "platform": "Windows", "help": "Uses lower disk scheduling priority to reduce disk contention, which can slow the scan."}];
var phpScanWindows = true;
/* Console JScript compatible: no JSON dependency, eval, credentials or target selection. */
var PhpScan = (function () {
    function parameters(values) {
        var fields = phpScanFields, selected = {}, index, field, text, number, multiplier, minimum, maximum;
        for (index = 0; index &lt; fields.length; index++) {
            field = fields[index];
            text = String(values[field.key]);
            if (field.text) {
                // Encode UTF-8 bytes, never interpolate a directory into script code.
                if (/[\x00-\x1f\x7f]/.test(text)) { throw new Error('Exclusions cannot contain control characters.'); }
                var entries = text.split(','), clean = [], j, entry, encoded, hex = 'x', k, byte;
                for (j = 0; j &lt; entries.length; j++) {
                    entry = entries[j].replace(/^\s+|\s+$/g, '');
                    if (!entry) { continue; }
                    var prefix = phpScanWindows ? /^([A-Za-z]:[\\\/]|\*[\\\/])/ : /^(\/|\*\/)/;
                    var relative = phpScanWindows ? /(^|[\\\/])\.{1,2}([\\\/]|$)/ : /(^|\/)\.{1,2}(\/|$)/;
                    if (!prefix.test(entry) || relative.test(entry)) {
                        throw new Error('Use absolute exclusion paths or a leading */; . and .. segments are not allowed.');
                    }
                    clean.push(entry);
                }
                if (clean.length &gt; 32) { throw new Error('Use at most 32 directory exclusions.'); }
                encoded = encodeURIComponent(clean.join(','));
                for (k = 0; k &lt; encoded.length; k++) {
                    if (encoded.charAt(k) === '%') { byte = encoded.substr(k + 1, 2); k += 2; }
                    else { byte = encoded.charCodeAt(k).toString(16); if (byte.length &lt; 2) { byte = '0' + byte; } }
                    hex += byte.toLowerCase();
                }
                if (hex.length &gt; 8193) { throw new Error('Directory exclusions must fit within 4096 UTF-8 bytes.'); }
                selected[field.key] = hex;
                continue;
            }
            if (!/^[0-9]{1,9}$/.test(text)) { throw new Error(field.label + ': enter a whole number.'); }
            number = Number(text);
            multiplier = field.multiplier || 1;
            minimum = Math.ceil(field.min / multiplier);
            maximum = Math.floor(field.max / multiplier);
            if (number &lt; minimum || number &gt; maximum) { throw new Error(field.label + ': use ' + minimum + ' to ' + maximum + '.'); }
            number = number * multiplier;
            selected[field.key] = String(number);
        }
        return selected;
    }
    function prepare() {
        try {
            var values = {}, index, field;
            for (index = 0; index &lt; phpScanFields.length; index++) {
                field = phpScanFields[index];
                values[field.key] = field.checkbox ? (document.getElementById(field.key).checked ? '1' : '0') : document.getElementById(field.key).value;
            }
            var selected = parameters(values);
            if (typeof TakeSecureFixletAction === 'undefined' || typeof Relevance === 'undefined') {
                throw new Error('Open this content in the BigFix Console to use this settings form. API/WebUI launches use defaults unless action parameters are supplied.');
            }
            // These are ordinary, nonsecret action parameters. The Console
            // obtains the current Task's Action1; no XML or script is rebuilt.
            TakeSecureFixletAction(Relevance('id of current fixlet'), Relevance('id of current bes site'), 'Action1', selected, {});
        } catch (error) { alert('Cannot prepare scan. ' + error.message); }
        return false;
    }
    return {parameters: parameters, prepare: prepare};
}());
document.body.ontakeaction = function () { return PhpScan.prepare(); };
&lt;/script&gt;</Description>
    <Relevance>if (version of client &gt;= "9.5.7") then (if windows of operating system then (windows of operating system and x64 of operating system and (if product type of operating system = nt workstation product type then version of operating system &gt;= "10.0.22000" as version else if product type of operating system = nt server product type or product type of operating system = nt domain controller product type then version of operating system &gt;= "10.0.14393" as version else false)) else false) else false</Relevance>
    <Category>PHP Security Discovery</Category>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to run bounded local PHP discovery.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">begin prefetch block
add prefetch item name=yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip sha1=344da50ce1693edd32b92c7d32eaf26d99c97f17 sha256=eac36a58699b94d3732a7fe1d8453fe89e0077bb18ac2c99b4c2ee102a431f2e size=9081400 url=https://github.com/VirusTotal/yara-x/releases/download/v1.22.0/yara-x-v1.22.0-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip
end prefetch block
action uses file encoding UTF-8 NoBOM
action uses wow64 redirection false
if {not exists parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex"}
parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = "x"
endif
continue if {length of parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" &lt;= 8193 and parameter "PHPExcludeDirectoriesHex" = regex "x([0-9A-Fa-f][0-9A-Fa-f])*"}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames"}
parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeNonstandardNames" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations"}
parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeBroaderLocations" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText"}
parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPIncludeBuildText" as integer) &lt;= 1}
if {not exists parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds"}
parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" = "1200"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" as integer) &gt;= 30 and (parameter "PHPEnumerationSeconds" as integer) &lt;= 3600}
if {not exists parameter "PHPScanSeconds"}
parameter "PHPScanSeconds" = "900"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPScanSeconds" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPScanSeconds" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPScanSeconds" as integer) &gt;= 30 and (parameter "PHPScanSeconds" as integer) &lt;= 3600}
if {not exists parameter "PHPMaxFiles"}
parameter "PHPMaxFiles" = "5000000"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPMaxFiles" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPMaxFiles" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPMaxFiles" as integer) &gt;= 1000 and (parameter "PHPMaxFiles" as integer) &lt;= 5000000}
if {not exists parameter "PHPCandidateGB"}
parameter "PHPCandidateGB" = "30"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPCandidateGB" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPCandidateGB" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPCandidateGB" as integer) &gt;= 1 and (parameter "PHPCandidateGB" as integer) &lt;= 100}
if {not exists parameter "PHPMaxFileMB"}
parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" = "512"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" as integer) &gt;= 16 and (parameter "PHPMaxFileMB" as integer) &lt;= 2048}
if {not exists parameter "PHPCpuLimit"}
parameter "PHPCpuLimit" = "10"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPCpuLimit" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPCpuLimit" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPCpuLimit" as integer) &gt;= 1 and (parameter "PHPCpuLimit" as integer) &lt;= 50}
if {not exists parameter "PHPGentleDisk"}
parameter "PHPGentleDisk" = "0"
endif
continue if {parameter "PHPGentleDisk" = regex "[0-9]+" and length of parameter "PHPGentleDisk" &lt;= 9}
continue if {(parameter "PHPGentleDisk" as integer) &gt;= 0 and (parameter "PHPGentleDisk" as integer) &lt;= 1}
parameter "output" = "{pathname of parent folder of data folder of client}/YARA_PHP"
parameter "work" = "{parameter "output"}/work-{id of action}"
folder create "{parameter "output"}"
folder create "{parameter "work"}"
delete __createfile
createfile until END_PHP_YARA_0f68f1276f3d50db
/*
  PHP install detection + version, all OSes (Linux ELF, Windows PE, macOS Mach-O).

  Deliberately broad: PHP_Binary_Broad flags anything that looks PHP-related so
  nothing is missed; the other rules carry the exact version string. Run with
  `yara -s` (or `yr scan -s`) to print the matched version text.

  Rules:
    PHP_Runtime_Version     - PHP core runtime; $ver holds the exact version,
                              incl. distro suffix (e.g. 8.1.2-1ubuntu2.27)
    PHP_Windows_VersionInfo - any PE whose version resource says ProductName=PHP
                              (php.exe, php-cgi.exe, php8ts.dll, ext\php_*.dll);
                              $pv holds ProductVersion
    PHP_Binary_Broad        - catch-all: any executable with any PHP marker
    PHP_Build_Artifact      - php-config / php_version.h left by source installs

  No modules are imported so the rules also work in embedded YARA engines
  (osquery, EDRs) that are built without the pe/elf/macho modules.

  See README.md for tested samples and the API number -&gt; branch table.
*/

private rule PHP_Detect_IsExecutable
{{
  condition:
    uint32(0) == 0x464C457F                                 // ELF
    or uint16(0) == 0x5A4D                                  // PE (MZ)
    or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACE or uint32(0) == 0xFEEDFACF   // Mach-O 32/64
    or uint32(0) == 0xCEFAEDFE or uint32(0) == 0xCFFAEDFE   // Mach-O 32/64, byte-swapped
    or uint32(0) == 0xBEBAFECA                              // Mach-O universal (CAFEBABE)
}

rule PHP_Runtime_Version
{{
  meta:
    description = "PHP core runtime (CLI/CGI/FPM/mod_php/libphp/php*ts.dll/php8.dll/embedded); $ver = exact version"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // Compile-time literal "X-Powered-By: PHP/" PHP_VERSION in main/SAPI.c.
    // Present regardless of expose_php. Suffix covers distro builds (8.1.2-1ubuntu2.27)
    // and pre-releases (8.5.0RC1).
    $ver = /X-Powered-By: PHP\/[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}/
  condition:
    PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and $ver
}

rule PHP_Windows_VersionInfo
{{
  meta:
    description = "Windows PE with PHP version resource; $pv = ProductVersion (exact version)"
    confidence = "high"
  strings:
    // UTF-16LE "ProductName" &lt;NUL + 0-2 bytes alignment pad&gt; "PHP\0"
    $pname = {{ 50 00 72 00 6F 00 64 00 75 00 63 00 74 00 4E 00 61 00 6D 00 65 00 [2-4] 50 00 48 00 50 00 00 00 }
    $pv = /ProductVersion\x00[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.\-]{{0,20}/ wide
  condition:
    // #pv &gt;= 0 is always true: $pv is only there so -s prints the version
    uint16(0) == 0x5A4D and $pname and #pv &gt;= 0
}

rule PHP_Binary_Broad
{{
  meta:
    description = "Broad catch-all: executable containing any PHP runtime/extension marker"
    confidence = "medium"
  strings:
    $xpb    = "X-Powered-By: PHP/"
    $zend   = "Zend Engine v"
    // ZEND_MODULE_BUILD_ID, e.g. API20220829,NTS / API20250925,TS - also in extensions
    $api    = /API20[0-9]{{6},N?TS/
    $pname  = {{ 50 00 72 00 6F 00 64 00 75 00 63 00 74 00 4E 00 61 00 6D 00 65 00 [2-4] 50 00 48 00 50 00 00 00 }
    $grp    = "The PHP Group" ascii wide
    $ini    = "php.ini"
    $fmt    = "PHP %s (%s)"
  condition:
    PHP_Detect_IsExecutable and
    (
      $xpb or $zend or $api or $pname
      or ($grp and ($ini or $fmt))
    )
}

rule PHP_Build_Artifact
{{
  meta:
    description = "php-config script or php_version.h header from a PHP build/install; $v* = version"
    confidence = "medium"
  strings:
    // php-config (installed next to the php binary by `make install` and -dev packages)
    $cfg_ver   = /version="[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}"/
    $cfg_a     = "php_cli_binary="
    $cfg_b     = "--php-binary"
    // main/php_version.h
    $hdr_ver   = /#define PHP_VERSION "[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,2}\.[0-9]{{1,3}[0-9A-Za-z.+~_-]{{0,40}"/
    $hdr_a     = "#define PHP_MAJOR_VERSION"
  condition:
    filesize &lt; 64KB and
    (
      ($cfg_ver and $cfg_a and $cfg_b)
      or ($hdr_ver and $hdr_a)
    )
}
END_PHP_YARA_0f68f1276f3d50db
delete "{parameter "work"}/php-detect.yar"
move __createfile "{parameter "work"}/php-detect.yar"
delete __createfile
createfile until END_PHP_YARA_318980fafe61de1e
#Requires -Version 5.1
param([string]$Archive,[string]$ArchiveHash,[string]$Destination,[string]$EngineHash)
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
Import-Module (Join-Path $PSHOME 'Modules\Microsoft.PowerShell.Utility\Microsoft.PowerShell.Utility.psd1') -ErrorAction Stop
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $Destination) {{ throw 'Engine destination exists' }
if ((Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $Archive -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant() -ne $ArchiveHash) {{ throw 'Archive hash mismatch' }
Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem
$zip = [IO.Compression.ZipFile]::OpenRead($Archive)
try {{
    $entry = $zip.GetEntry('yr.exe')
    if (-not $entry -or $entry.Length -gt 64MB) {{ throw 'Unexpected archive entry' }
    [IO.Compression.ZipFileExtensions]::ExtractToFile($entry,$Destination,$false)
}
finally {{ $zip.Dispose() }
if ((Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $Destination -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant() -ne $EngineHash) {{ throw 'Engine hash mismatch' }
